-- Fixture for "l4 batch reads back a BREACH BY a list in a left-nested RAND".
--
-- `l4 batch` re-prints the module and checks it again. The printer writes
-- (a RAND b) RAND c without its brackets, and the parser reads that back as
-- a RAND (b RAND c), so the BREACH BY LIST below, the second operand as
-- written, is the FIRST operand of the inner RAND in the module batch
-- checks. With no GIVETH, the PARTY operand before it fixes the party type
-- either way. (The adversarial pass of 2026-11-20: F4 without a GIVETH.)

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Alice, Bob, Carol, Dave
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF deliver, notify, exercise

`root` MEANS
    ((PARTY Carol MUST deliver WITHIN 3) RAND (BREACH BY LIST Alice, Bob BECAUSE "x")) RAND (PARTY Dave MUST notify WITHIN 4)

#TRACE `root` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Dave DOES exercise AT 20

@export default trivial entrypoint so batch has a function to call
alwaysTrue MEANS TRUE
